cer-only market on its scheduled Wednesday or Saturday. Treat it as a browse-and-orient stop; purchases are optional.","short_summary":"A recurring open-air farmers market in downtown Market Square.","evidence_claim":"The Market Square Farmers' Market is a producer-only open-air market held Wednesdays and Saturdays from May through October.","source_url":"https://www.knoxvilletn.gov/workspaces/one.aspx?contextId=123284&objectId=21242666","source_title":"Market Square Farmers Market","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2026-06-03","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"This recurring market is scheduled Wednesday and Saturday, not Sunday; confirm the current listing and weather before planning around it.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"market-square","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Market Square","title":"Pause in Market Square","subtitle":"Sunday afternoon • Between Wall and Union avenues","notes":"Use the square and adjacent Krutch Park as a downtown waypoint. Look at the old Market House bell and suffrage monument, then check the city calendar for public events.","short_summary":"A downtown public square with event space, a fountain, and nearby Krutch Park.","evidence_claim":"Market Square lies between Wall and Union avenues, is adjacent to Krutch Park, and hosts special events, live music series, and seasonal farmers markets.","source_url":"https://www.knoxvilletn.gov/government/city_departments_offices/special_events/market_square_info","source_title":"Market Square Info - City of Knoxville","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor civic space; event setups and seasonal programming may affect access.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"south-college","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"South College","title":"Close with a historic-campus loop","subtitle":"Sunday late afternoon • The Hill","notes":"Walk by South College from public paths and compare it with nearby Ayres Hall. Use the university’s historic-building guide to add context without entering restricted spaces.","short_summary":"A preserved historic building on the Hill, near Ayres Hall.","evidence_claim":"South College remains on its original site on the Hill and originally served as a dormitory and campus armory for East Tennessee University.","source_url":"https://torchbearer.utk.edu/2019/08/10-historic-buildings/","source_title":"10 Historic Buildings","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2019-08-22","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View from public campus paths; do not assume interior access.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":["The farmers market is a Wednesday/Saturday activity, so it is included as a seasonal alternate rather than a literal Sunday stop. Check current university, museum, and city schedules before visiting."]}],"warnings":[]}
